      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The 640‑acre mission founded in 1838, three miles north of Toledo, was the first Catholic mission in Washington state.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.historylink.org/File/23363",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Every July, Toledo celebrates its dairy roots with Cheese Days, featuring a giant cheese ball drop on New Year’s Eve.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toledo%2C_Washington",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Kemp Olson Memorial Park, the city’s main park, honors a long‑time fire chief and hosts community events.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toledo%2C_Washington",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Founded in 2004, the Toledo Historical Society preserves local history and now occupies a former library space that received a grant for a children’s area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
